# L §2.3 bandrow = qid ["[" key "]"] ":" … (tally 2.1.6, issue #88): a band row's key is a key, never *, so
# `b[*]: [20, inf) = 6` is refused at parse. tally 2.1.5's refcore read it as a row key and printed its node's name
# (LOAD-KEY star is not a key of classes).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
index classes = [c1, c2]
band b[k in classes](n: int): int
input x: int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  b[c1]: [0, 10) = 1
  b[c1]: [10, inf) = 2
  b[c2]: [0, 20) = 5
  b[*]: [20, inf) = 6
  x = 12

ask q1: b[c1](x), b[c2](x), band_hi(b[c2], x) law 2026-06-30
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE cannot parse: expected a literal, got * (m.tally:19)
